{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And YHWH came down to see.</b> Note that the expression 'to come down to see' is said of the blessed El when the matter is not yet worthy of punishment — but rather because of the corruption that ultimately follows from it — as in the rebellious and defiant son, concerning whom the Sages said: 'The Torah descended to the end of his intent.' So too was the matter of Sodom, concerning which it is written: אֵרְדָה נָּא וְאֶרְאֶה (Genesis 18:21), for indeed their wickedness was not then greater than that of the other nations so as to warrant punishing them in this world — except in the matter of cruelty toward the poor of the nation, from which complete corruption would ultimately follow, as it says: הִנֵּה זֶה הָיָה עֲוֹן סְדֹם וְגוֹ' (Ezekiel 16:49). So too was the punishment of Israel in their exile, as it says: אֶרְאֶה מָה אַחֲרִיתָם (Deuteronomy 32:20)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:49.140529734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}